---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Notes on third-party and game content
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Website source (HTML, CSS, JS for the library shell and apps in this
  repository) is covered by the license above unless otherwise noted.
- Individual games and tools may include their own LICENSE or NOTICE files
  inside their folders. Respect those terms separately.
- Graphics, icons, and cover art created for this project are original
  project assets unless a file or page credits another source.
- Do not assume that third-party fonts, images, audio, or code you add later
  are covered by this MIT license; keep clear attribution and licenses for
  those assets.

- Live China public-holiday lookups (optional, when online) may use the
  public Nager.Date API (https://date.nager.at/). That data is not part of
  this MIT-licensed source tree; the API’s own terms apply to live fetches.
- Bundled fallback holiday lists and original game/tool code in this repo
  remain under the MIT terms above unless a subfolder states otherwise.

- Optional client-side TTS under assets/tts/:
  - Piper voice models from rhasspy/piper-voices (MIT) — see each voice
    folder and assets/tts/VOICES.md.
  - ONNX Runtime Web, piper-phonemize, and related browser helpers are
    third-party MIT-licensed components; see assets/tts/VOICES.md.
  - Browser speechSynthesis voices are provided by the user’s operating
    system / browser and are not redistributed as part of this license.

- This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by the International
  Baccalaureate Organization. IB PYP reference material in tools is an
  unofficial classroom aid for teachers.
